(2)
Every process for which an exhaust draught is required shall be carried on inside a suitable hood.
(3)
Air discharged from exhaust ventilating plant used in connection with any of the processes specified in clause 3 (1) shall,
whether or not it has been passed through dust collecting apparatus, be discharged directly into the open air from where
it is not liable to be drawn into the air of any work-room.

61. Precautions during caustic grinding, etc. - Every machine used for grinding or crushing caustic shall be enclosed;
and an efficient exhaust draught shall be provided where any of the following processes are carried on :-
(i)
Grinding or crushing of caustic;
(ii)
